<title>UK: BRITISH ELECTION DIARY - April 22.</title>
<headline>BRITISH ELECTION DIARY - April 22.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the election diary for Tuesday, April 22:</p>
<p>LONDON - Labour party leader Tony Blair, Shadow Chancellor Gordon Brown and Shadow Small Business Minister Barbara Roche give daily party briefing at 8.30 a.m. (0730 GMT)</p>
<p>Blair then sets off on campaign tour in afternoon ending with rally in Stevenage.</p>
<p>- Conservative party holds daily news briefing at 9.15 a.m. (0815 GMT)</p>
<p>Prime Minister John Major sets off on another day of campaigning outside London.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +4471 542 7950</p>
